  'm3.q93': ['Wet pipe is the most common system, used where there is no risk of freezing.', 161],
  'm3.q94': ['Water is always in the pipes right above the heads, so it reaches the fire straight away.', 161],
  'm3.q95': ['In a dry pipe system the pipes hold pressurised air. When a head opens, the air pressure drops and that opens the control valve.', 161],
  'm3.q96': ['An alternate system is water-filled for summer, then drained and filled with pressurised air for winter. It suits unheated buildings.', 161],
  'm3.q97': ['Pre-action pipes hold air, and water only enters when a detector (such as a smoke detector) operates.', 161],
  'm3.q98': ['Deluge and recycling systems are not strictly sprinklers and are only used in special industrial cases.', 161],
  'm3.q99': ['Mist cools flame and gases by evaporation, displaces oxygen by evaporation, and the tiny droplets block radiant heat.', 162],
  'm3.q100': ['Water mist is increasingly used in big data rooms and flammable liquid stores, and widely in the marine sector.', 162],
  'm3.q101': ['An open head nozzle simply propels water out and is usually triggered by automatic fire detection (AFD).', 162],
  'm3.q102': ['Cylinder systems, for smaller risks, hold a mix of water and nitrogen near the room.', 162],
  'm3.q103': ['Openings for new pipework must be as few and small as possible, sealed to at least the wall or floor\'s required performance.', 162],
  'm3.q104': ['Some fire retardants and plasticisers in fire-stopping have reacted with CPVC pipes and fractured them. Follow the pipe maker\'s guidance.', 163],
  'm3.q105': ['BS 9251 covers sprinklers for residential and domestic occupancies. BS EN 12845 is the general automatic sprinkler standard.', 164],
