  'm3.q112': ['Escape route signs are green, with white text or symbols.', 166],
  'm3.q113': ['A fire exit route is provided specifically for a fire emergency. An exit route is one people use and know every day.', 166],
  'm3.q114': ['"Fire door keep shut" is a mandatory instruction sign: a blue circle with white text, something you must do.', 167],
  'm3.q115': ['A mandatory notice combines several instructions: mandatory (blue), evacuation (green) and prohibitive (red).', 167],
  'm3.q116': ['Firefighting equipment location signs are red with white text and symbols.', 167],
  'm3.q117': ['Warning signs, a yellow triangle, identify nearby danger.', 167],
  'm3.q118': ['Wayfinding signs in high-rise residential stairwells help the fire and rescue service identify floors in smoke and low light.', 167],
  'm3.q119': ['Wayfinding signage is compulsory on residential buildings with more than three storeys, or an upper storey over 11m.', 167],
